        <p>WONDKRFUL DISCOVERY.—This is' the age ti of research and exreriment, when all nature, so to speak, is ransacked by the aelentific for the comfort and happinesa of man. Science has indeed made giant strides during the past century, and among the —by no means least importatt—discoverles in medicine comes that of THRRAFIOI7 This preparation is unquestionably one of the most genuine and reliable Patent Medicines ever Introduced, and nos we understand, been used in the Continental Hospitals by Ricord, Itostan, Jobert, Velpeau, Malsonnenve the well- known Chastaignae, and indeed by all who are regarded as authorities in such matters. including the celebrated Lallemand, and Roux, by whom It was some time sinoe uniformly adopted. and that it worthy the attention of those who require such a remedy we think there is no doubt. From the time of Aristotle downwards a potent agent in the removal of these diseases has (like the famed philo opher'e stone) been the object of search of some hopeful generous minds ; and far beyond tbe mere power—if such could ever have been discovered—of transmuting the baser metals foto gold is surely the discovery of a remedy so potent as to re- plenish the falling energies in the one case, and in the other so effectually. speedily and safely to expel from the system the poisons of acquired or inherited disease In all their potent forme as to leave no taint or trace behind. Such is the new French Remedy THRRAPION, which may certainly rank with, if not take precedence of, many of the discoveries of our day, about which no little ostentation rn4 noise have been made, and the extensive and ever-mcreasing demand that has been created for this medicine wherever Introduced appears to prove that ills destined to cast into oblivion all those questionable remedies that were formerly the sole reliance of medical men. Therapion may be obtained of the principal chemists unit merchants throughout the world.— " Diamond Fields Advertiser."—Kimberley.—For particulars of Iherapion, send stamped, addressed envelope to MR. R JcIINSON, 43, HOLFORD EQ , LONDON, W.O.</p>
