      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-09-02_WidnesExaminer_art0021" n="art0021">
        <head>IVIIS. ARTHUR PAGST.</head>
        <p>IVIIS. ARTHUR PAGST.</p>
        <p>Mrs. Arthur Paget has endless patience and pluck, and, not coutent with her recovery, which is complete to a certain extent, she is next month to undergo another serious operation, which, if successful, will allow her to walk as well as she did before without either crutches or stick. The operation is exceedingly difficult, and the Onfooker hears that the patient will be kept throe hours under chloroform.</p>
        <p>TO-DAY'S RECIPE.</p>
        <p>CIIAMPIONONS ' FARCIS AU POISSON. Takn SORIA firm mushrooms, remove the stalks and the soft part of the inside; throw them with the stalks into boiling water with a good deal of lemon juice in it, and let them boil for five minutes. Now take them out and let them drain thoroughly. Take some fillets of sole and simmer them in strong fish stock; when they are thoroughly cooked, mince them up very finely with the mushroom stalks. Put the mince into a stewpan with a large lump of butter, salt, neoner. and some strong meat gravy or beef ,SSCIIOO, aria conic it tor rwenty minutes over slow fire. Fill the mushrooms with this farce and pour over them a Pechamel sauce with plenty of lemon juice in it; put them into tlas Gaga for ten minutes and servo. . , I,',</p>
