      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-09-02_WidnesExaminer_art0027" n="art0027">
        <head>'ATER POLO.</head>
        <p>'ATER POLO.</p>
        <p>• WARRINGTON V. WIGAN. Warrington played their concluding match of the season in connection with the Liverpool and District League in the Legh street baths on Tuesday, when they met the League champions. There was a large attend- ance to witness the fixture. Wigan on the first half defended the deep end and Pemberton obtained the ball and play was early in the visitors' quarters. A. Ashton was placed in a favourable position and sent in a hard shot, but Smith easily cleared. C. Ashton next worked his way to the visitors goal but nothing resulted. The visitors frequently pressed and Woods was several times called upon but he cleverly saved. After W. Ashton had shot over the bar, the visitors got within easy distance of the Warrington goal and Hodson succeeded in defeating Woods. Half-time, Wigan one goal, War- rington nil. In the second half, Wigan had practically their own way and goals Nsore scored by Smith (21, Saunders (2), Hodson and Nevison (ono each). C. Ashton had on one occasion very hard lines in not scoring, the visiting custodian luckily clearing. He, however, managed to pnt one through from long range, and was heartily cheered. Final : Wigan,seven goals; Warrington one goal. SECOND DIVISION. WARRINGTON 2ND V. BIRKENHEAD.—This match was also decided at Warrington on Tuesday. Warrington defended the deep end in the first half, and the visitors early pressing and Leyland scored with a swift shot. Turner next got possession and dribbling up to the goal scored easily. Barker was next tested, but he sent clear to Boscow who transferred to Wilkinson and the Latter scored. A penalty was afterward granted to Birkenhead, and from the ensuing scrimmage Stocks</p>
      </div>
