        <p>The health of little children and babies is subject to rapid changes, and careful mothers should not delay at the first sign of feverishness, with chills or flushes. There is warning in a hot dry skin, thirst, quick breath- ing and a plaintive cry; at such a time a prompt dose of Peptolaxa, the children's friend, will avert serious illness. Mrs. Talbot, 18, Violet-street, Halifax, has proved this in her family. She writes: "I am convinced Peptolaxa warded off a fever or other serious disease in its first stage, and my child was saved from a long illness. My John, aged 5 was taken ill suddenly with Feverishness ; his whole body became like a furnace. He vomited food, was terribly restless all night, and did nothing but cry. He could hardly raise his head. I had heard of wonderful cures by Peptolaxa and gave him two tablets which acted easily on his bowels, and he enjoyed peaceful sleep. On waking, he took food, mended rapidly, and attended school again."</p>
