      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-09-02_WidnesExaminer_art0043" n="art0043">
        <head>PENKETH.</head>
        <p>PENKETH.</p>
        <p>LIBER L CLlJB.—Members, and those desirous of joining, should note that the Club room is now re-opened after the renovations and decoration, and it looks extremely well. The work has been in the hands of Mr. H. J. Mainley, and has been favourably commented upon.</p>
        <p>In memory of Capt. and Adjutant Edward Usher; of the Royal Scots Greys (2nd Dragoons), who• was mortally wounded at Klippan in the Transvaal on 13th February, 1902, a handsome brass tablet has been placed in Great Budworth parish church, Cheshire. The firstateam motor-car on the London and North- Western Railway was run on Saturday for the official opening of the Dyserth Railway. The car left Ethyl with a select party, and reached the pretty mountain village of Dyserth in twenty-five minutes.</p>
      </div>
