      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-09-02_WidnesExaminer_art0095" n="art0095">
        <head>EXAMPLE.</head>
        <p>EXAMPLE.</p>
        <p>Nothing is so contagious as exaniple—be it good or bad. Never was iere any considerable good iisr ill done that did not produce its like. We imitate good actions through emulation, and bad ones through malignity in our natures; this shame conceals, until example sets it at liberty. AN IGNORANT BOY.</p>
        <p>Bobby: What is the meaning of " riot trans- ferable." Papa?</p>
        <p>Papa: I ant surprised •at your ignorance, 'iobert. It means that you are not adm4tted /less you go yourself.</p>
