        <p>Wycliffe P.S.A. Society. 00 There was a good attendance at this meeting' Sunday last when Mr. Farrar presided and spoke uP've the best thing worth knowing : "To know we, 16'10d, eternal life." The mind of man, the great gift 0, sfic he said, was always longing to know more. Sir Is by Newton said he was only like one picking Pebblesoe the sae shore while the ocean was before hifl. more one knows the more one feels he does not !'0„11c1 It was a great thine to know God's Fatherhooa test love, to know Christ's power to save, but the grea thing to know was that we had eternal life throutre Christ. Mr. C. F. Fooks, of Manchester, speaker and spoke upon " Sitting on the fence,' be• urged the brethren to be decided for one side 01.1.1'6 , other. If God be God serve Him. The Secre—to welcomed five new members and asked all presentarst bring new members next Sunday as it was the was Sunday in the new half-year. A vote of sy passed to the widow and family of one of tbe who has passed away after a long illness. Mr. u°"the The Rev.J. Yonge,and Mr.C.Cotton also took part meeting. A favourite hymn of the late and now deco:nct brother," Knocking, knocking," was very feelinglS 'Te W M impressively sung. Mr. .H. Payton, Mos. Dec.,Bac., P sided at the organ. mpathyber9</p>
